[size=6][b]♦ They Bleed[/b][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/TheyBleedOpenMW/main/imgs/they_bleed_banner.png[/img]

The spoils of war taint your surroundings; your violence now leaves bloodied marks on the environment. Low-HP players/NPCs also leave subtle blood trails.

[url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/TheyBleedOpenMW/main/imgs/head_like_a_hole_banner_left_half_bright148.webp[/img][/url][url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/TheyBleedOpenMW/main/imgs/nexus/banner_right.png[/img][/url]
[url=https://ko-fi.com/maxyari][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MaxYari/TheyBleedOpenMW/main/imgs/nexus/banner_glow.png[/img][/url]

[size=5][b]♦ How to install[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Requires OpenMW 0.51 or newer.[/b]
[*]Install it like any other OpenMW mod and enable [font=Courier New]TheyBleed.omwscripts[/font] in the "Content Files" tab of the OpenMW launcher. If this is your first OpenMW mod, [url=https://modding-openmw.com/tips/installing-mods/]read this tutorial[/url].
[*]Settings are in Options -> Scripts -> They Bleed.
[/list]

The blood comes with PBR maps made for [url=https://github.com/wareya/OpenMW-PBR]Wareya's PBR shaders[/url], so it looks wet and glossy with them. It [i]might[/i] (or might not) look wrong with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/53667]Rafael's shaders[/url] or other shaders that read these maps differently. If the blood looks off, delete the [font=Courier New]*_spec.dds[/font] files from [font=Courier New]textures/MaxYari/TheyBleed/[/font] (they hold the metalness and roughness). The normal maps ([font=Courier New]*_n.dds[/font]) are fine and can stay.

To uninstall, set "Max Decals" to 0 and save your game first, so no blood is left behind in your save. Then uninstall the mod.

[size=5][b]♦ Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/morrowind/mods/45368]Diverse Blood[/url] is supported: blue, green, dark and orange blood leave decals of matching colour. Dust, sparks and energy leave none.
[*]Should work with any mod that doesn't replace OpenMW's built-in combat blood effect.
[/list]

[size=5][b]♦ AI disclaimer[/b][/size]

Made with HEAVY AI assistance. Only this mod's logo was made completely by human hands, and, well, I also picked out myself that little sound that you might hear when the blood droplets hit the environment. The rest was just working with a coding AI, testing and correcting.
